From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:05:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: t8132: Power a gated DCP up before a
 timing change

An audit of every path that can reach the internal DCP outside a frame
found two more that can run while it is power-gated after a blank.

A commit that lights the display with another timing (a refresh-rate
change in the same commit as DPMS on, for example) sends the new mode
from iomfb_m4_atomic_mode(). That runs before the frame that would
power the DCP up, so the call goes to the stopped CPU and fails the
session, as the colour paths did. Power the DCP up first, as the frame
would. A blank followed by a mode change then behaves as before the
power-down existed.

The flight work of an asynchronous swap drained the mailbox while
gated, with RX held. Let it only wait out its deadline there.

Paths found already safe:
 - backlight work, brightness keys, XDR wind-down: they need a shown
   frame, which a blank clears;
 - idle cache: it needs the display on;
 - runtime idle work and resume: they check gated already;
 - HDR metadata: state only, no call;
 - debugfs: read-only;
 - external DCPs: an idle-gated one is powered up by the call path
   itself, and a sleep-gated one by resume before any request.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 8b6b798337..28480b18ca 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -2468,7 +2468,14 @@ static void dcp_m4_int_fl_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	int ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&dcp->lock);
-	if (r->int_fl.open) {
+	/* Powered down: RX is held and nothing arrives; the deadline still ends it. */
+	if (r->int_fl.open && READ_ONCE(dcp->gated)) {
+		if (time_after_eq(jiffies, r->int_fl.deadline))
+			dcp_m4_int_flight_lost(r, -ETIMEDOUT);
+		else
+			queue_delayed_work(r->wq, &r->int_fl_work,
+					   max_t(long, (long)(r->int_fl.deadline - jiffies), 1));
+	} else if (r->int_fl.open) {
 		ret = READ_ONCE(dcp->error) ?: dcp_m4_runtime_drain(r, 32);
 		if (r->int_fl.open && (ret < 0 || time_after_eq(jiffies, r->int_fl.deadline)))
 			dcp_m4_int_flight_lost(r, ret < 0 ? ret : -ETIMEDOUT);
@@ -4676,6 +4683,17 @@ int iomfb_m4_atomic_mode(struct apple_dcp *owner, const struct drm_display_mode
 	if (want->id == READ_ONCE(r->live_id))
 		return 0;
 	mutex_lock(&dcp->lock);
+	/*
+	 * A commit that lights the display with another timing reaches here before
+	 * the frame that powers a gated DCP up: power it up first, as that frame would.
+	 */
+	if (dcp->gated) {
+		ret = iomfb_m4_power_ungate(dcp);
+		if (ret) {
+			mutex_unlock(&dcp->lock);
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
 	ret = dcp_m4_int_set_mode(dcp, want, &status);
 	if (!ret && !status) {
 		WRITE_ONCE(r->live_refresh_16_16, want->refresh_16_16);
-- 
